                ================================
                = RELEASE NOTES OF BHWIDE 1.07 =
                ================================
		
--------------------------
What's NEW in VERSION 1.07
--------------------------

* A new version of hadronic vacuuum polarization added - option: KeyPol = 4.
  Routines of F. Jegerlehner, 21.10.2025; see bhw/repi.f: chadr5x25().
* A new function for leptonic vacuum polarization; see bhw/repi.f: REPILE(S).
* SM parameters (masses, widths, constants) updated according to PDG 2025.

--------------------------
What's NEW in VERSION 1.06
--------------------------

* Obsolete Fortran instructions and statements replaced with the ones accepted
  by newer gfortran compilers, in particular GNU Fortran 13.2.0.
* Modifications in Makefiles and their structure: multiple Makefile.templ
  in subdirectories replaced with a single Makefile.inc in the main directory.
* Updated EW parameters (masses, widths, constants) according to PDG 2024.
  
--------------------------
What's NEW in VERSION 1.05
--------------------------

* A weight corresponding to pure QED corrections is calculated also for 
  KeyEWC = 1 with KeyLib = 2. This speeds up considerably computation of
  pure weak corrections, which can be taken as a difference between the
  EWC weight and the QED weight, see README for details.

--------------------------
What's NEW in VERSION 1.04
--------------------------

* The bug in the routine IMZ2 of ALIBABA's EWC library causing a crash
  of the program above the tt~ threshold has been fixed.
  Now BHWIDE can be run safely for CMS energies above the tt~ threshold.

--------------------------
What's NEW in VERSION 1.03
--------------------------

* The bug in the routine FILBHW that did not allow for low cuts 
  on the final electron energy (below ~0.3GeV for LEP energies) 
  has been fixed (thanks to Martin Gruenewald). 
  NOTE: It did not affect the physical results for the allowed cuts.

--------------------------
What's NEW in VERSION 1.02
--------------------------

* The following parameters: 
    WTMAX  - Maximum Weight for rejection
    AMAZ   - Z mass 
    GAMMZ  - Z width
    SINW2  - sin^2(theta_W)
    AMTOP  - top quark mass 
    AMHIG  - Higgs     mass
  are now added to the INPUT parameters (no more hidden in the code);
  see description of INPUT for details.
* A possibility of switching-off Z-contribution added with the help
  of a key: KeyZof =0/1 (Z-contr. ON/OFF) - for tests only!
* One can choose pure t or pure s channel contributions with the help
  of a switch: KeyCha =0/1/2 (s+t/s/t contributions) - for tests only!
* Compiler flags can be easily updated in all subdirectories with the help
  of Makefile in the main directory - see README.
* Programming bugs/exceptions that caused problems on some computers
  have been fixed. 

--------------------------
What's NEW in VERSION 1.01
--------------------------

* Added the new option: "QED corrections + vacuum polarization" 
                        (KeyEWC=0, KeyPia=1,2,3; see the program). 
  This may be useful for lower energies where the Z contribution
  and the weak corrections are small (it increases an efficiency
  of MC generation considerably). For this option both the BABAMC
  and ALIBABA virtual corrections libraries should be equivalent.
* Real part of the photon vacuum polarization in ALIBABA routines
  replaced by more recent calculations (with 3 options: KeyPia=1,2,3).




